  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 244 PM CDT Sat Aug 1 2026\n\nA segment of the upper low in Canada will intensify along the \nnational border and tilt negatively across North Dakota and \nMinnesota. We'll see the effects of its cold front as early as \nTuesday afternoon, lasting through Wednesday. Instability over 1000 \nJ/kg sets up in the warm sector, but with favorable deep-layer \nshear lagging behind the boundary. Flow will be parallel to the \nboundary and PWATs will rise above 1.5\", so there will be heavy \nrain potential in northern Iowa due to moisture content and\ntraining storms. This risk is currently represented with a \nMarginal Excessive Rainfall Outlook.\n\nIowa will stay in cyclonic flow through the remainder of the week \nwhich will keep precipitation chances and cooler temperatures in \nplay.",
